OL,3,CCorrespondence with TV news presenter
OL,4,CNatalie Graham
OL,5,
OL,6,GDID YOU ALWAYS WANT TO GET INTO
OL,7,GJOURNALISM AND JOIN THE BBC?
OL,9,F"No, I wanted to be a psychologist but
OL,10,Fthen pivoted into journalism in 1995
OL,11,Fand found it suited me perfectly. I am
OL,12,Fnow combining both with my off-air work
OL,13,Fat the BBC."
OL,23,EPub: 15-Jan-2026Upppppppppppppppppppppp
OL,24,ANext Page BShowreel  CRewind FNat Radio
FL,143,140,120,200,0,100
PN,14203
SC,0003
CT,3,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F142A1786056662
OL,1,W~s1z5~k4j5jw=hw1~sj5           G3/6
OL,2,W,.!/*%+.!+.-'*%/"-$+,"-$U,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,3,CCorrespondence with TV news presenter
OL,4,CNatalie Graham
OL,5,
OL,6,GWHAT DID YOU DO AT BBC SOUTHERN
OL,7,GCOUNTIES RADIO?
OL,9,F"I worked in Guildford. I spent the
OL,10,Ffirst nine months in the newsroom then
OL,11,Fbecame the district reporter for
OL,12,FCrawley in 1997/1998.
OL,14,F"I then moved to Brighton to work on
OL,15,Fthe Brighton and Sussex breakfast shows
OL,16,Fas the 'live reporter' until I moved
OL,17,Finto TV."
OL,23,EPub: 15-Jan-2026Upppppppppppppppppppppp
OL,24,ANext Page BShowreel  CRewind FNat Radio
FL,143,140,120,200,0,100
